## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of consent-driven data minimization, offline safety, and the relationship between consent lifecycle and CCA score calculation.

## Key Concepts
- Consent tokens gate data exposure
- policy_version controls exposure granularity
- Idempotent, offline-safe compute operations
- Per-user data retention settings

## Code Example
```javascript
async function computeCCA(userIdMasked, consentToken, policyVersion) {
  const consent = await consentStore.validate(consentToken, policyVersion);
  if (!consent?.allowed) {
    throw new Error('Not authorized');
  }
  const score = await calculateScore(userIdMasked, consent);
  return { user_id_masked: userIdMasked, cca_score: score };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests practical edge compute handling: budget-aware routing, deterministic fallbacks, and testability in real apps.

## Key Concepts
- Budget-aware orchestration: enforce per-request time budgets for compute paths
- Deterministic fallback: seed heuristic with user_id_masked and client_timestamp for reproducibility
- Telemetry: track latency, fallback usage, and model_version for auditing
- Testability: budget-bound tests, fairness across devices, end-to-end reproducibility

## Code Example
```javascript
function selectScore(input){
  const {budgetMs, start}=input;
  const canRunModel = simulateModelCost(input) <= budgetMs;
  if(!canRunModel){
    return heuristicScore(input.user_id_masked, input.client_timestamp);
  }
  return modelScore(input);
}
```

